      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. For most inpatients it is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make this dose safe, and a higher dose gives no added analgesic benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another regimen\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that it was intentional. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
